Q7 — Data Quality Check: Detect Anomalies Before Loading
---------------------------------------------------------

Before loading orders_cdc into the warehouse, your pipeline runs
a data quality gate. Write a single query that checks ALL of the
following and returns one row per failed check:

1. NULL order_id — must never be null
2. amount <= 0 — orders must have positive amount
3. status not in allowed values ('pending','delivered',
   'cancelled','returned')
4. updated_at in the future (> CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
5. Duplicate order_id + updated_at + op combinations
   (true duplicates that DISTINCT won't catch if any field differs)


QUERY:
------
WITH checks AS (

    SELECT 'null_order_id' AS check_name,
           COUNT(*) AS failed_rows
    FROM orders_cdc
    WHERE order_id IS NULL

    UNION ALL

    SELECT 'invalid_amount',
           COUNT(*)
    FROM orders_cdc
    WHERE amount <= 0

    UNION ALL

    SELECT 'invalid_status',
           COUNT(*)
    FROM orders_cdc
    WHERE status NOT IN ('pending','delivered','cancelled','returned')

    UNION ALL

    SELECT 'future_timestamp',
           COUNT(*)
    FROM orders_cdc
    WHERE updated_at > CURRENT_TIMESTAMP

    UNION ALL

    SELECT 'duplicate_cdc_rows',
           COUNT(*) - COUNT(DISTINCT CONCAT(order_id,'|',
                                            CAST(updated_at AS CHAR),'|',
                                            op))
    FROM orders_cdc
)
SELECT check_name, failed_rows
FROM checks
WHERE failed_rows > 0;


TRAP:
-----
The duplicate check using CONCAT is fragile — if order_id contains
the delimiter character '|' you get false matches. In production
use a composite GROUP BY with HAVING COUNT(*) > 1 instead:

    SELECT 'duplicate_cdc_rows',
           COUNT(*) AS failed_rows
    FROM (
        SELECT order_id, updated_at, op
        FROM orders_cdc
        GROUP BY order_id, updated_at, op
        HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
    ) dups

Also: this query returns ZERO rows if all checks pass — which is
exactly what you want. Wire this into your pipeline as a gate:
if row count > 0, fail the pipeline and alert.

EXPECTED OUTPUT (with sample data):
| check_name         | failed_rows |
|--------------------|-------------|
| duplicate_cdc_rows | 2           |

(O002 and O003 each have one duplicate INSERT)


