Q10 — Full Pipeline Audit: End-to-End Reconciliation
-----------------------------------------------------

At end of day your pipeline must reconcile: rows in source
(orders_cdc raw count) vs rows in clean table (orders_clean)
vs rows in aggregate (daily_revenue). Any mismatch must be flagged.

Write a single query that produces a reconciliation report showing:
- raw CDC rows loaded today
- unique orders after deduplication
- orders in orders_clean
- delivered orders counted in daily_revenue aggregate
- any row count mismatches flagged with a reason


QUERY:
------
WITH raw_counts AS (
    SELECT
        DATE(updated_at)    AS pipeline_date,
        COUNT(*)            AS raw_rows,
        COUNT(DISTINCT order_id) AS distinct_orders_in_raw
    FROM orders_cdc
    GROUP BY DATE(updated_at)
),
clean_counts AS (
    SELECT
        DATE(updated_at)    AS pipeline_date,
        COUNT(*)            AS clean_rows
    FROM orders_clean
    GROUP BY DATE(updated_at)
),
agg_counts AS (
    SELECT
        revenue_date        AS pipeline_date,
        total_orders        AS agg_orders
    FROM daily_revenue
),
reconciliation AS (
    SELECT
        rc.pipeline_date,
        rc.raw_rows,
        rc.distinct_orders_in_raw,
        COALESCE(cc.clean_rows, 0)  AS clean_rows,
        COALESCE(ac.agg_orders, 0)  AS agg_orders,
        CASE
            WHEN rc.distinct_orders_in_raw != COALESCE(cc.clean_rows, 0)
                THEN 'MISMATCH: dedup count != clean table'
            WHEN rc.raw_rows = rc.distinct_orders_in_raw
                THEN 'WARNING: no duplicates found — verify CDC source'
            ELSE 'OK'
        END AS reconciliation_status
    FROM raw_counts rc
    LEFT JOIN clean_counts cc ON rc.pipeline_date = cc.pipeline_date
    LEFT JOIN agg_counts   ac ON rc.pipeline_date = ac.pipeline_date
)
SELECT * FROM reconciliation
ORDER BY pipeline_date;


TRAP:
-----
The WARNING case ("no duplicates found") sounds like a good thing
but in a CDC pipeline it is suspicious. Real transactional systems
almost always have at least some UPDATE events — if you see zero
duplicates across millions of rows, either your deduplication ran
twice (already cleaned upstream) or the CDC tool is misconfigured
and sending only INSERTs. Always sanity check the op column
distribution: what % are INSERT vs UPDATE vs DELETE. A 100% INSERT
rate on a CDC feed is a red flag.

EXPECTED OUTPUT:
| pipeline_date | raw_rows | distinct_raw | clean_rows | agg_orders | status                              |
|---------------|----------|--------------|------------|------------|-------------------------------------|
| 2024-03-01    | 5        | 4            | 2          | 1          | MISMATCH: dedup count != clean table|
| 2024-03-02    | 5        | 4            | 2          | 2          | MISMATCH: dedup count != clean table|
| 2024-03-03    | 2        | 1            | 0          | 0          | MISMATCH: dedup count != clean table|

All three dates show mismatch because orders_clean only has 2 rows
(partial load from crashed pipeline). This is exactly what the
reconciliation report should catch and alert on.


